**When to read this file:** When you add or gate code that touches files, network, OS, hardware, UI, or security — and always when you edit `std/src/ooda/` (see `BOOTSTRAP.oot` tier *Security, sandboxing, capability gating* + `DESIGN.oot` §3).

*Update this list when a token is added or fractured. Keep count note in sync with DESIGN. Prefer granular tokens in new APIs. CAP-G1/G2 preferred maps are path-A process-local seal contracts. CAP-G3 is residual-only honesty (exact require stubs; **no** HW/UI product ops). CAP-G3 inject path-A landed. CAP-G4 ProcessCap path-A FIXED. CAP-G5: process-local only (no product seccomp). **CAP-G6 not FIXED:** sample fs/net product facades prefer granular; **SysCap bulk residual** + ProcessCap std = 0; no push until C2.*
